## Upstream lineage

Fluxora is an independent product. It is not an official release of, and does
not claim any affiliation with, any upstream project.

Fluxora's codebase is derived from **bettbox+**
(<https://github.com/Tiam9173/bettboxplus>, v1.19.2, commit `dcad2db`), which is
distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. bettbox+ is in turn a
rebuild of **Bettbox** (<https://github.com/appshubcc/Bettbox>).

Fluxora's independent product identity — branding, UI, design tokens, theming,
and the Windows loopback component — was developed on top of that base starting
2026-09-25 (commit `7d47c3f`).

## Bundled components

- **Mihomo (Clash.Meta)** — the proxy core. Licensed GPL-3.0; the licence text
  is at `core/Clash.Meta/LICENSE` and the corresponding source is in `core/`.
- **Flutter / Dart packages** — their licence texts are collected automatically
  by the Flutter tool and shipped inside the application bundle as
  `data/flutter_assets/NOTICES.Z`.
- **Fluxora Loopback Manager** (`windows/fluxora_loopback/`) — original work,
  Copyright (C) 2026 Fluxora Contributors, GPL-3.0-or-later.

## Historical third-party binary (removed)

Earlier revisions of this repository included a third-party Windows loopback
exemption tool at `windows/WindowsLoopbackManager.exe`, obtained from
`appshubcc/Windows-Loopback-Manager` (author: `tiagonmas`).

The upstream project does not publish a licence for that binary, so its licence
status is unknown. It has therefore been removed from this repository and is no
longer distributed in any form.

Its function is now provided by Fluxora's own implementation,
`FluxoraLoopbackManager`, built from `windows/fluxora_loopback/`. That component
is an independent implementation and is the only loopback tool shipped.

For audit traceability, the removed file was:

    path   : windows/WindowsLoopbackManager.exe
    size   : 197120 bytes
    sha256 : d9b1bd0e9f05c8f046578c6f870b1c6822fbd660a01c55a4c838386432215263

